{
  "id": "Compound::DB00195 - Disease::DOID:10763",
  "verbalization": "Betaxolol is implicated in the treatment of hypertension through a chain of interactions involving beta-adrenergic antagonists. The evidence suggests that Betaxolol, through its treatment of glaucoma, is linked to timolol, a beta-adrenergic antagonist, which in turn treats hypertension. This pathway highlights a potential mechanism by which Betaxolol may exert its effect on blood pressure regulation, possibly through the modulation of beta-adrenergic signaling. The shared ancestry of Betaxolol with metoprolol, another beta-adrenergic antagonist, further supports this connection, as both compounds are part of a broader class of drugs that target the same biological pathway. The integration of these relationships underscores the role of beta-adrenergic antagonists in the therapeutic action of Betaxolol, suggesting a possible repositioning of Betaxolol for use in hypertension treatment.",
